A||N||5||Xtreme Fiero's||Power door locks||||5||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||09-14-2000||09:51 AM||||<BR>is there any way to adjust the power locks on our cars? I have to push the button like 3-5 times to unlock my doors. my pasenger side rarley works but they just click away and the manual lever just wiggles. Is there any thing I can lube to help em' out?||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||09-14-2000||09:57 AM||||Mine do the same thing.  I think they're just old and dirty.  A lot of cleaning and lubing probably will get them going again.  I haven't taken the time to try that though.  It's low on the  l o n g  priority list.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||09-14-2000||10:05 AM||||After I added power locks on my car I had the same problem.  Take the door panel back off and use some WD-40 or medium weight oil to lube the linkages back in the door latch assembly and any other connections.  Put some oil on that plastic guide thingy that the linkage slides against too.<P>Now, temporarily hook up the switch with the door panel off and look to see what's going on at the actuator when you flip the switches.  Even bending the linkage just a little can help it.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||09-14-2000||10:31 AM||||huggrrfiero: I'll try that this week end, Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||09-14-2000||03:05 PM||||I had the same problem when I got my car. I believe it's caused by not operating the power lock/unlock on a regular basis. I took the door panel off and used brake cleaner to loosen up the old grease then use white lithum spray grease to re-lub the locking mechanism. <P>After working the locks (with the electric switch) for about three weeks, they are both working pretty well. The passenger door lock still isn't 100% yet. I did notice that the pivot that is attached to the door frame was a little more sloppy on the passenger side then the driver side. I took a better one off of a parts car and the next time I remove the passenger door panel I plan to change it out.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000005||Carrolles||09-14-2000||03:58 PM||||Try spraying a little WD-40 directly on the actuator.  Let it dribble down the shaft into the servo.  This has worked on several of my cars.<P>Unless you see bent linkage the problem is usually the actual actuator getting bound up with corrosion.  The rubber boot that the shaft goes through lets a little moisture in.  <BR>||||reg||1
